    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0769" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/2–1750: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Israel</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McDonald</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tel Aviv</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-02-17T12:00:00+02:00">February 17,
                            1950—noon.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>119. At my request Shiloah with Kollek<anchor n="1" xml:id="d360-f1"/> at
                    residence, February 16 said he and possibly Dayan to meet with Abdullah and
                    Samir (Geneva <pb facs="0770" n="748" xml:id="pg748"/> for USPCC and USTC) night
                    February 17 in Transjordan. Shiloah’s letter of “few days ago” to Samir
                    recalling their agreement February 3 on another meeting was not answered; but
                    Shiloah’s later indirect approach to Samir was promptly accepted.</p>
                <p>Shiloah said he is not optimistic. Confident King still wants agreement but fears
                    he may not be able build Cabinet willing to take responsibility for agreement
                    with Israel. Shiloah credits Samir with intelligent, earnest desire secure
                    settlement and being willing risk much to get it.</p>
                <p>Information Shiloah gave me re Transjordan Cabinet meeting February 13 was
                    similar that Amman Legtel 10 February 13.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d360-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Comment:</hi> I believe Shiloah as usual is telling
                    truth but not necessarily whole truth. <hi rendition="#italic">End
                    comment</hi>.</p>
                <p>[Here follows the last paragraph, dealing with the health of Prime Minister
                    Ben-Gurion.]</p>
                <p>Sent Department 119, repeated Jerusalem 10, Department pass Geneva 1, London
                    29.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McDonald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d360-f1" n="1" xml:id="d360-f1-content">
                <p>Theodore (Teddy) Kollek, Director of the North American Division of the Israeli
                    Ministry for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d360-f2" n="2" xml:id="d360-f2-content">
                <p>This telegram was a repeat of No. 22 from Amman, <ref target="#pg741">p.
                        741</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
